== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [A wave of frequency 20 Hz has a wavelength of 15 m. Its speed is], [0.75 m s⁻¹], [35 m s⁻¹], [300 m s⁻¹], [3000 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(2, [Sound cannot be heard on the Moon because], [the Moon is too cold], [there is no atmosphere to carry it], [gravity is too weak], [light travels too fast])

#mcq(3, [The image formed by a plane mirror is], [real and inverted], [real and magnified], [virtual and laterally inverted], [virtual and magnified])

#mcq(4, [A ray passes from air into glass of refractive index 1.5 at 30°. The angle of refraction is], [19°], [30°], [45°], [60°])

#mcq(5, [An object 15 cm from a converging lens of focal length 10 cm forms an image at], [6.0 cm], [15 cm], [30 cm], [45 cm])

#mcq(6, [The colour deviated most by a glass prism is], [red], [green], [yellow], [violet])

#mcq(7, [A string 0.50 m long vibrates in its fundamental at 200 Hz. The speed of the wave is], [100 m s⁻¹], [200 m s⁻¹], [400 m s⁻¹], [800 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(8, [An echo from a wall 204 m away returns after 1.2 s. The speed of sound is], [170 m s⁻¹], [245 m s⁻¹], [340 m s⁻¹], [408 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(9, [A concave mirror of focal length 8.0 cm forms a real image at 24 cm. The object distance is], [6.0 cm], [12 cm], [16 cm], [24 cm])

#mcq(10, [The critical angle for glass of refractive index 1.5 is about], [30°], [42°], [49°], [60°])

#mcq(11, [The power of a lens of focal length 20 cm is], [0.20 D], [2.0 D], [5.0 D], [20 D])

#mcq(12, [The additive primary colours are], [red, yellow and blue], [cyan, magenta and yellow], [red, green and blue], [red, green and yellow])

#mcq(13, [A wave of wavelength 0.20 m and frequency 500 Hz travels at], [100 m s⁻¹], [250 m s⁻¹], [1000 m s⁻¹], [2500 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(14, [Two tuning forks of 440 Hz and 444 Hz are sounded together. The number of beats per second is], [2], [4], [8], [884])

#mcq(15, [A convex mirror always forms an image that is], [real and inverted], [virtual, upright and diminished], [virtual and magnified], [real and diminished])

#mcq(16, [A pool 4.0 m deep appears, to a person looking straight down, to be ($n = 1.33$)], [3.0 m deep], [4.0 m deep], [5.3 m deep], [6.0 m deep])

#mcq(17, [A telescope has an objective of focal length 120 cm and an eyepiece of 5.0 cm. Its magnification is], [5], [24], [60], [125])

#mcq(18, [Which of these travels fastest in a vacuum?], [radio waves], [visible light], [X-rays], [all travel at the same speed])

#mcq(19, [Two neighbouring nodes on a stationary wave are separated by], [one wavelength], [half a wavelength], [a quarter of a wavelength], [two wavelengths])

#mcq(20, [The pitch of a musical note depends on its], [amplitude], [frequency], [quality], [speed])

#mcq(21, [A ray strikes a plane mirror at 25° to its surface. The angle of reflection is], [25°], [50°], [65°], [90°])

#mcq(22, [When light passes from air into water, which quantity is unchanged?], [speed], [wavelength], [frequency], [direction])

#mcq(23, [Short sight is corrected with a], [converging lens], [diverging lens], [cylindrical lens], [plane mirror])

#mcq(24, [A red object viewed in green light appears], [red], [green], [black], [yellow])

#mcq(25, [The third harmonic of a string whose fundamental is 120 Hz has a frequency of], [240 Hz], [360 Hz], [480 Hz], [120 Hz])

#mcq(26, [A pipe closed at one end has a fundamental of 170 Hz. Its next resonance is at], [340 Hz], [510 Hz], [680 Hz], [850 Hz])

#mcq(27, [An object is placed at the focus of a concave mirror. Its image is formed], [at the focus], [at the centre of curvature], [at infinity], [behind the mirror])

#mcq(28, [A ray in glass strikes the boundary at 50°. If the critical angle is 42°, the ray], [is refracted into the air], [is totally internally reflected], [travels along the surface], [is absorbed])

#mcq(29, [Two thin lenses of powers $+4.0$ D and $-1.0$ D are in contact. The power of the pair is], [$+3.0$ D], [$+4.0$ D], [$+5.0$ D], [$+0.33$ D])

#mcq(30, [The illuminance 2.0 m from a lamp of intensity 40 cd is], [10 lux], [20 lux], [40 lux], [80 lux])

#mcq(31, [A water wave passes from deep water into shallow water. Which quantity is unchanged?], [speed], [wavelength], [frequency], [amplitude])

#mcq(32, [An echo returns from a cliff after 0.50 s. If the speed of sound is 340 m s⁻¹, the cliff is], [85 m away], [170 m away], [340 m away], [680 m away])

#mcq(33, [The focal length of a concave mirror of radius of curvature 40 cm is], [10 cm], [20 cm], [40 cm], [80 cm])

#mcq(34, [Snell's law may be written], [$n = sin r \/ sin i$], [$n = sin i \/ sin r$], [$n = sin i times sin r$], [$n = i \/ r$])

#mcq(35, [A diverging lens has a focal length of $-30$ cm. Its power is], [$+3.3$ D], [$-3.3$ D], [$-0.30$ D], [$+0.30$ D])

#mcq(36, [Compared with the other members of the electromagnetic spectrum, radio waves have], [the shortest wavelength], [the highest frequency], [the longest wavelength], [the same wavelength as X-rays])

#mcq(37, [Two identical waves travelling in opposite directions produce], [a progressive wave], [a stationary wave], [no wave at all], [a beat])

#mcq(38, [As a source of sound approaches a stationary observer, the observed frequency], [rises], [falls], [stays the same], [falls to zero])

#mcq(39, [The mirror used as a shaving mirror is], [plane], [convex], [concave], [cylindrical])

#mcq(40, [Dispersion by a prism occurs because the refractive index depends on], [the angle of incidence], [the colour of the light], [the thickness of the prism], [the shape of the prism])

